      "publication_date": "2020-01-01",
      "abstract": "This paper argues that the work of the young Luk\u00e1cs can be read as a wide-ranging mediation on what I am labelling \u203athe crisis of subjectivism\u2039. Reading Luk\u00e1cs this way allows us to see important continuities between his pre-Marxist and Marxist period. Most significantly, it allows us to see how positing the proletariat as a \u203asubject-object\u2039 of history and developing a crisis diagnosis of bourgeois society, allowed Luk\u00e1cs to bring the fruits of his earlier intellectual labour under conceptual control.",
